1
00:00:01,080 --> 00:00:02,777
.n

2
00:00:02,860 --> 00:00:04,977
.v

3
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,200
Thank you.

4
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:36,960
I guess it's my turn to fill you guys in.

5
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:41,277
First, we have a close call with these
twin-metal dinosaur-looking creatures.

6
00:01:41,360 --> 00:01:44,457
Then, when we were about to crash
for the night, wouldn't you know it?

7
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:47,057
We're camped out right on top of a big,

8
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:50,316
wicked serpent thing who goes
by the name of Seadramon.

9
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:52,277
That's when things got intense.

10
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:57,420
I got snatched up and Goblumon digivolved
into a huge blue wolf called Garurumon.

11
00:01:57,960 --> 00:02:00,580
Lucky for me, Seadramon was no match.

12
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:04,680
Whenever we're in danger, our
Digimon get bigger and help us.

13
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:06,240
Now that's cool.

14
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:12,430
Shagunetsu!

15
00:02:12,513 --> 00:02:13,343
Birdramon!

16
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:32,457
oh hey whoa did you hear that it seems

17
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:34,517
to be some sort of aircraft it looked

18
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:38,337
like a big flying gear admit it my
alien theory is becoming more plausible

19
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:42,177
yeah they hit us with an anti-gravity
ray to make us all crooked or maybe that

20
00:02:42,260 --> 00:02:46,677
sign's just crooked hey that was scary

21
00:02:46,760 --> 00:02:50,160
watch it That could have
been a snake, or worse.

22
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:52,200
Oh, boy, I'm sorry.

23
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:56,120
Hey, Beelmon, are there
really snakes here?

24
00:02:56,400 --> 00:03:01,200
No, just giant flying killer bugs
and other unpleasant Digimon.

25
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:03,260
Don't you worry, TK.

26
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:04,893
I'll take care of that.

27
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:10,137
Okay, now that that's
settled, let's get going.

28
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:12,057
Nothing's settled, and where would we go?

29
00:03:12,140 --> 00:03:13,437
We don't even know where we are.

30
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:14,350
This is silly.

31
00:03:14,433 --> 00:03:18,417
I say we keep moving and see if we can
find any signs of intelligent life here.

32
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:19,780
Hey, wait a minute.

33
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:22,900
Is he saying that Digimon
are not intelligent?

34
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:24,711
Is that what he's saying?

35
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:26,917
Not at all, but I think Tai is right.

36
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,977
We need to keep moving in hopes
of finding out where we are.

37
00:03:30,060 --> 00:03:32,413
We need to stay calm and stick together.

38
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:35,297
Let's remember, we're in this together.

39
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:37,440
Together sounds good. We can do it.

40
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:38,477
This will take teamwork,

41
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:41,797
and I'm sure we'll figure out exactly
where we are and how to get back.

42
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:46,397
There's no point in splitting up because
then once somebody did figure it out...

43
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:48,780
Hey, Sora, open your eyes.

44
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:51,160
Well, thanks a lot for waiting.

45
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:53,057
Moving right along, folks.

46
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:54,022
Keep it moving.

47
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:57,937
Our next stop on the tour will be
the forest of irrelevant road signs.

48
00:03:58,020 --> 00:03:59,196
No pictures, please.

49
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:04,397
We're lost and these guys are
making jokes. Hey, wait up.

50
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:05,517
My shoelace is broken.

51
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:06,820
You need new shoes.

52
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:08,277
Ooh, new shoes.

53
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:09,260
Look,

54
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:12,037
telephone poles I say
we follow them and see

55
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:14,877
where they lead They'll
just lead to trouble Look,

56
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:18,784
it's the alien saucer again And
it's headed for a close encounter

57
00:04:21,620 --> 00:04:26,080
Why, it's so hot I can feel the heat
coming up through my socks Well, TK,

58
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:28,694
maybe you should put your shoes back on

59
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:36,737
Oh, this hot desert air is destroying
my complexion How much further is it?

60
00:04:36,820 --> 00:04:38,497
Is that all you're worried about, Mimi?

61
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:40,657
We'll be lucky if we
even survive this hike.

62
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:41,570
Hey,

63
00:04:41,653 --> 00:04:46,117
does anybody besides me see that these
telephone poles have no connecting wires?

64
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,120
She's right.

65
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:49,697
I wonder if these actually
are telephone poles.

66
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:52,133
Maybe they're some odd alien equivalent.

67
00:04:52,220 --> 00:04:56,580
Hey, remember those phone
booths and that streetcar? Yeah?

68
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,760
What about them? Oh, nothing.

69
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:02,060
I was just wondering if
anybody else remembered.

70
00:05:02,820 --> 00:05:04,320
That's it. Doomed.

71
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:08,157
The heat has baked our brains, and we're
all going to end up like roasted piglets?

72
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:09,417
Just remain calm, Joe.

73
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:11,177
We've only been walking for two minutes.

74
00:05:11,260 --> 00:05:12,660
Izzy, come here, Izzy.

75
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:16,260
I think we'd better find some
shade for Joe. And quick.

76
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:21,017
You won't believe what
happened to my favorite watch.

77
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:21,930
Hmm? What?

78
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:24,660
The sun melted the numbers right off.

79
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:29,218
Mimi, for somebody who hates hiking,
you sure have a lot of compasses.

80
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,795
Of course, none of them actually work.

81
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:36,377
Oh, this dirt contains small traces of
metal which could affect the compass needle.

82
00:05:36,460 --> 00:05:38,237
Oh, well, I'm always late anyway.

83
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:41,657
This is one weird world, and I
don't like it one little bit.

84
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:43,937
I think we should start
looking for water, guys.

85
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:46,457
Otherwise, we could
dehydrate in all this heat.

86
00:05:46,540 --> 00:05:47,370
Yeah.

87
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:50,480
But we're doing okay
for now, aren't we? Yay!

88
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:55,700
Somebody please find us!

89
00:06:03,520 --> 00:06:06,457
I've taken a soil sample,
measured the barometric pressure,

90
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:08,137
and analyzed the relative humidity.

91
00:06:08,220 --> 00:06:09,749
And what did you find out?

92
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:12,440
It's really, really hot.

93
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:15,266
Hang on just a little longer.

94
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:16,539
Don't give up now.

95
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:18,737
We're going to be okay.

96
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:20,137
Just keep moving along.

97
00:06:20,220 --> 00:06:21,279
My head is baking.

98
00:06:21,620 --> 00:06:24,997
If this goes on too much longer, I'm
going to look like a wilted salad.

99
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:26,757
Here, you wear my hat for a while.

100
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:28,428
You need it more than I do.

101
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:30,260
Thank you, Mimi.

102
00:06:31,620 --> 00:06:32,600
Hey, you!

103
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:34,272
What's that yucky smell?

104
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:37,454
Ugh, here's a thought.

105
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:40,248
Now you know why they
call them sweat socks.

106
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:44,157
This beach would be a lot more popular
if it just had a couple more things,

107
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:45,200
like an ocean,

108
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:48,640
a gentle breeze, snack
bar, Hong lifeguards.

109
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:51,360
Hold it, I have to stop.

110
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:54,628
I just don't think that
I can go any faster.

111
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:56,920
You have to stay positive.

112
00:06:57,240 --> 00:06:59,358
Let's all pretend that it's raining.

113
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:00,590
Yeah!

114
00:07:00,673 --> 00:07:01,503
That's a great idea.

115
00:07:01,586 --> 00:07:02,912
I simply adore the rain.

116
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:05,657
Me too, but it's time for a reality check.

117
00:07:05,740 --> 00:07:06,997
This isn't getting any better.

118
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:10,797
It might be a good idea to turn around
and get out of this desert right now.

119
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:13,237
You mean before we all
have a power outage?

120
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:14,150
I'll vote for that.

121
00:07:14,233 --> 00:07:15,063
Wait.

122
00:07:15,146 --> 00:07:16,896
Hold on for just a second, everybody.

123
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:20,900
If I'm seeing what I think I'm
seeing... What is it, Tide?

124
00:07:21,820 --> 00:07:23,100
It's not a mirage.

125
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:25,140
It's real water. Water?

126
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:26,760
This is fantastic.

127
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:30,117
Now all we need are some lemon,
sugar, and some big, fat ice cubes.

128
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:31,297
That looks like a village.

129
00:07:31,380 --> 00:07:32,537
Maybe we'll find people.

130
00:07:32,620 --> 00:07:33,620
And Shaggy.

131
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:35,437
Maybe they'll have hats for sale.

132
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:36,350
Hang on.

133
00:07:36,433 --> 00:07:37,263
Water and food.

134
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:39,277
I'm hungry enough to eat broccoli.

135
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:40,257
What's broccoli?

136
00:07:40,340 --> 00:07:41,222
Is that a joke?

137
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:42,550
Great.

138
00:07:42,633 --> 00:07:43,777
Let's get out of this desert.

139
00:07:43,860 --> 00:07:44,690
Yay!

140
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:10,577
from so far away everything looks
so big but they're so cute and tiny

141
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:14,717
okay question who here knows where
we can get a drink and just what do

142
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:19,357
giant digimon drink me i'm no digimon
my friend sora is what's called

143
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:22,757
a human being yes we know they look
funny in spite of this they're all

144
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:27,817
actually very nice if you are not
to g mom what are you doing here in

145
00:08:27,900 --> 00:08:33,857
this is great there is no way we're
all gonna fit into this place relax

146
00:08:33,940 --> 00:08:37,797
joe at least the natives here are
friendly oh my i would just love to

147
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:41,880
take one home and put it on my bed
with all my other stuffed animals

148
00:08:42,180 --> 00:08:45,237
there she goes again do you
think mimi hears the same

149
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:49,540
things we hear i'm not sure
anymore Maybe she's an alien spy.

150
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:51,380
KK is tired and hungry.

151
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:53,000
He's not the only one.

152
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:56,640
Beelon, just when did you digivolve?

153
00:08:56,740 --> 00:09:00,157
When I met Sora, we share a
special bond, which is magical.

154
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:02,037
You don't talk like us anymore.

155
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:03,757
Is that how all Beelon talk?

156
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:05,664
No, it's how the big ones talk.

157
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:08,097
I suppose I just picked it up from Sora.

158
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:11,957
She is a wonderful and kind human being,
and I've already learned a lot from her.

159
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:13,997
We still don't understand
how you digivolved.

160
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:14,910
Digivolved?

161
00:09:14,993 --> 00:09:18,477
What is it about being around
human beings that makes it happen?

162
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:19,580
Zora needed me.

163
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:21,155
I had to protect her.

164
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:24,917
When she was in danger, a
power came flowing through me.

165
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,700
Wait a sec. Now I get it.

166
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:28,617
That's why she's always
following me around.

167
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:30,677
All of a sudden, I
realized I had Digivolved.

168
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:34,525
When Tai needed him, Agumon
Digivolved to Greymon to protect him.

169
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:36,717
And Garurumon did the same for Matt.

170
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:38,400
They Digivolved for us.

171
00:09:39,140 --> 00:09:40,400
We're lucky kids.

172
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:43,477
Zora, we're invited to
have dinner with the Yokos.

173
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:46,097
They said they'd be willing to
share their food with all of us.

174
00:09:46,180 --> 00:09:47,010
Oh, wow.

175
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:48,290
Yay!

176
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:50,017
Let's see hands if you want lemonade.

177
00:09:50,100 --> 00:09:51,760
I wonder what Yokomon eats.

178
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:53,957
I'll take a cheeseburger,
fries, and a shake.

179
00:09:54,040 --> 00:09:55,997
I wonder what they will be serving.

180
00:09:56,080 --> 00:10:00,320
Perhaps some bone with meat, lettuce
topped with fish, or... Water!

181
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:02,030
Water?

182
00:10:02,113 --> 00:10:04,800
Look, everybody, a fresh
water fountain. Hooray!

183
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:08,657
All of the water here is piped in
from a spring at Miharashi Mountain.

184
00:10:08,740 --> 00:10:10,157
It's the best water in the world.

185
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:14,299
Forget the world, Mount Miurashi
water is the best in all the galaxy.

186
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:16,500
Where's Mount Miurashi? Out there!

187
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:18,808
Hey, that's a live volcano.

188
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:21,469
Yes, but the heat boils
away all the germs.

189
00:10:26,580 --> 00:10:29,698
If I'm not mistaken, that
noise precedes an eruption.

190
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:34,268
That's cool, but I still
didn't get a drink.

191
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:35,860
What is happening?

192
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:37,580
The water evaporated.

193
00:10:37,860 --> 00:10:40,448
That's okay because the
lake is always full.

194
00:10:40,660 --> 00:10:41,719
I'll check it out.

195
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:42,690
Let's all go.

196
00:10:44,620 --> 00:10:46,080
The water's all gone.

197
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:48,040
Goodness, where did it go?

198
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:49,891
Somebody pulled the plug.

199
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:51,988
All right, let's not panic.

200
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:58,040
Dry as a bone. I won't give up.

201
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:06,281
Ty's doing a little dance for us.

202
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:08,697
Is that supposed to sound the
fire or bring down the rain?

203
00:11:08,780 --> 00:11:12,200
Hey, do you remember that
flying gear we saw earlier?

204
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:14,460
It crashed right into a hillside.

205
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:15,830
Great.

206
00:11:15,913 --> 00:11:19,397
Of all the hillsides out there, the
gear crashes into Miharashi Mountain.

207
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:21,677
That's the place where
the water comes from.

208
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:22,590
That's right.

209
00:11:22,673 --> 00:11:25,197
The water comes from a lake
on the top of Mount Miharashi.

210
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:28,597
So a gear crashing into the mountain
could affect our water supply.

211
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:29,510
Mm-hmm.

212
00:11:29,620 --> 00:11:31,149
We don't dare go up there.

213
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:34,751
The mountain is guarded by a
fiery Tichimon called Meramon.

214
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:36,557
He's hideously dangerous.

215
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:39,120
I want a closer look at that mountain.

216
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:42,397
You say this character
Meramon is a fiery Digimon?

217
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:43,833
What does he look like?

218
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:45,700
Never mind, there he is!

219
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:46,740
He's coming!

220
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:47,937
He's coming our way!

221
00:11:48,020 --> 00:11:49,977
He burns up everything he touches!

222
00:11:50,060 --> 00:11:52,357
He never comes down off the mountain, Mo!

223
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:55,740
This is very strange behavior for him! Ah!

224
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:57,800
I'm burning too hard!

225
00:11:58,100 --> 00:11:59,900
Meramon is a fiery Digimon.

226
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:03,517
There's no reason he should be
in pain from his own flames.

227
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:04,659
That's his nature.

228
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,240
This is weird.

229
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:10,460
He's crying.

230
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:14,460
Burning, burning, burning, burning!

231
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:18,849
Sounds like he's out
of his mind with pain.

232
00:12:19,020 --> 00:12:19,880
What do we do?

233
00:12:20,180 --> 00:12:22,480
Burning, burning, burning!

234
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:43,077
Look, he's coming straight
toward the village.

235
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:45,377
Hey, everybody, we better
decide what we're going to do.

236
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:46,917
I've never seen him move so fast.

237
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,417
He's already reached the
foot of the mountain,

238
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:50,971
and now he's starting to enter the forest.

239
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:52,259
Everybody, freeze.

240
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:53,760
Stay very still.

241
00:12:56,620 --> 00:12:59,679
You're going to need more
than sunscreen to stop me.

242
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:01,800
Don't move a muscle.

243
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:07,560
Burn! Burn! Burn!

244
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:11,800
Universe!

245
00:13:15,260 --> 00:13:16,720
And run!

246
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:43,377
Come on, keep it moving.

247
00:13:43,460 --> 00:13:44,989
All the way from the rear.

248
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:46,179
Okay, settle down.

249
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:47,337
There's room for all of you.

250
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:49,244
Will you please stop squirming?

251
00:13:51,060 --> 00:13:52,707
Here's the next batch, Matt.

252
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:55,530
Easy now.

253
00:13:55,613 --> 00:13:56,443
You'll be okay.

254
